  "notes": "～{続|つづ}ける is an auxiliary verb meaning \"to continue doing.\"\n\nPATTERN:\nVerb stem + {続|つづ}ける\n\nEXAMPLES:\n- {読|よ}み{続|つづ}ける: to continue reading\n- {待|ま}ち{続|つづ}ける: to keep waiting\n- {走|はし}り{続|つづ}ける: to keep running\n- {働|はたら}き{続|つづ}ける: to keep working\n- {歩|ある}き{続|つづ}ける: to keep walking\n\nNUANCE:\n～{続|つづ}ける emphasizes sustained, persistent action over time. Often implies effort or determination.\n\nCONTRAST:\n- ～{続|つづ}ける: continued action (emphasizes persistence)\n- ～ている: ongoing state (simple progressive)",
